{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00017",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.76,
      "end_seconds": 6.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "Doctor, I've brought them through. The observations are done, whenever you need them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.34,
      "end_seconds": 12.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Hi, how can I help today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 14.35,
      "end_seconds": 19.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "Morning, um, doctor. I'll stay and fill in anything that's missed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.45,
      "end_seconds": 26.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 26.97,
      "end_seconds": 33.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.26,
      "text": "It's a bit of discharge, doctor. She didn't wanna come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.49,
      "end_seconds": 37.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "when did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.14,
      "end_seconds": 42.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "About about a month, give or take."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 48.11,
      "end_seconds": 52.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Hm, I'd say more like about two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.88,
      "end_seconds": 57.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly one to two months. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.98,
      "end_seconds": 75.71,
      "duration_seconds": 15.73,
      "text": "Yeah, roughly. I've also had muffled hearing on that side. About muffled hearing on that side, I'd give it a six, out of ten. I've also had a feeling of blockage, since last weekend."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.75,
      "end_seconds": 80.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "And how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.36,
      "end_seconds": 107.75,
      "duration_seconds": 26.39,
      "text": "About a six out of ten. Oh, and pain when I move my jaw. That's been about the same, about two weeks. With pain when I move my jaw, it feels moderate to me. Honestly, once or twice a day. Yes, chewing. That makes it worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.32,
      "end_seconds": 113.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.32,
      "end_seconds": 119.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Yes, eczema."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.43,
      "end_seconds": 126.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "And apart from that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.79,
      "end_seconds": 129.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "I've got diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.39,
      "end_seconds": 136.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "okay, I can see eczema and diabetes in your file as well"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.08,
      "end_seconds": 154.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.7,
      "end_seconds": 174.39,
      "duration_seconds": 17.69,
      "text": "I've never smoked. I have a couple of drinks on the weekend. I drive a delivery van all day. Yes, I live on my own. I go to the gym a couple of times a week"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.53,
      "end_seconds": 189.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Right, are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.22,
      "end_seconds": 198.23,
      "duration_seconds": 8.01,
      "text": "Hydrocortisone cream, when needed for the eczema. I'm on glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.01,
      "end_seconds": 203.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "What about allergies, to to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.28,
      "end_seconds": 208.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.5,
      "end_seconds": 214.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "And what about swelling behind the ear, recent cold or ringing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.98,
      "end_seconds": 218.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "No. None of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.93,
      "end_seconds": 220.8,
      "duration_seconds": 0.87,
      "text": "Any dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.95,
      "end_seconds": 225.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any dizziness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 226.22,
      "end_seconds": 231.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "actually, doctor, I did notice dizziness she doesn't always say"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.56,
      "end_seconds": 238.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.13,
      "end_seconds": 247.09,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and and what you've noticed. Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.22,
      "end_seconds": 250.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "No weakness or anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 250.82,
      "end_seconds": 259.3,
      "duration_seconds": 8.48,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pulse is 80 beats a minute, temp 36.9 degrees, pressure 117 over 73, saturation 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.07,
      "end_seconds": 261.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.66,
      "end_seconds": 266.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "So, I'd like to examine you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.11,
      "end_seconds": 270.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "okay, bear with me a second"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.19,
      "end_seconds": 286.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "I can't see the eardrum properly because of the swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.63,
      "end_seconds": 290.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "right, tell me if anything hurts"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.87,
      "end_seconds": 310.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "The ear canal is red and swollen with some debris, and pulling the ear hurts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.06,
      "end_seconds": 314.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "thanks for that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.98,
      "end_seconds": 341.79,
      "duration_seconds": 9.81,
      "text": "Okay, thinking it through, I don't have a clear answer today: an outer ear infection is possible, and so is a middle ear infection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.82,
      "end_seconds": 346.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "What are the chances it's something bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.8,
      "end_seconds": 364.27,
      "duration_seconds": 17.47,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like an outer ear infection. We'll begin with ciprofloxacin ear drops, three times a day, for seven days. That should help with outer ear infection"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 366.34,
      "end_seconds": 370.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Should I keep taking it if I feel better?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.29,
      "end_seconds": 383.76,
      "duration_seconds": 11.47,
      "text": "Keep water out of the ear and don't use cotton buds. I'd like you back if it's not better in four days. Ask me anything before you go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 384.81,
      "end_seconds": 387.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Alright, thanks. Bye for now."
    }
  ]
}